            <ArticleTitle>[Double blind clinical study of local immunotherapy in treatment of periodontal diseases].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>197-209</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>During a 3 weeks period, an immunotherapy by oral route was applied in patients presenting periodontal diseases (gingivitis and chronic adult periodontitis). This study, double blindly conducted, points out a statistically significative decrease of the main clinical symptoms of periodontal diseases (bleeding, erythema, oedema, pain, suppuration, fetidness) without any other local treatment and shows the interest of such a therapy in addition to the classical local treatments applied to patients presenting periodontal diseases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
